-- The LDSS worker is working to coordinate a Fit-to-parent evaluation for Ms. Saint Fleur. The local worker communicates with Ms. Saint Fleur regarding Rose''s medical, physical, and developmental needs. The Local Department worker meets with Ms. Saint Fleur to discuss service planning, and enters into service agreements with her. ","permToPermExpln":"Not applicable.","safeAndCareExpln":"The LDSS worker visits Rose on at least a monthly basis. The worker also completes additional visits when transporting Ms. Saint Fleur to see Rose. The LDSS worker coordinates care with Second Family staff, ensuring that Rose gets to her specialist appointments. The LDSS worker also ensures that SSI payments and insurance issues are resolved in a timely manner. The LDSS worker has met with Rose''s pediatrician to evaluate Rose''s need for 1:1 care and to address concerns about Rose''s neurological development. ","assessmentPeriodExpln":"The LDSS worker offers weekly transportation to Ms. Saint Fleur to visit Rose. The LDSS worker also transported Ms. Saint Fleur to Rose''s cardiology appointment on July 17th. The LDSS worker met with Ms. Saint Fleur in her home on September 6th to discuss service planning. The LDSS worker has networked with various providers to inquire about Fit to Parent evaluation services.  ","lifebookExpln":"Not yet, pictures continue to be collected. ","serviceAgreementExpln":"Ms. Saint Fleur consistently accepts phone calls from the Department and is an active participant in conversations. She communicates with the Department regarding her goals and desires for reunification. She reports being highly motivated to reunify with her daughter. She, and the LDSS worker have created a service plan that includes goals such as visiting at least once per week, obtaining a cognitive evaluation, training with Second Family staff to care for Rose, going to Rose''s appointments, obtaining a more spacious living arrangement, and obtaining reliable transportation.","isProvi